// Seed Code Mail — Cloudflare Workers configuration
// ============================================================================
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
//
// `npx wrangler deploy` was failing with:
//
//     [ERROR] Error parsing file: /opt/buildhome/repo/vite.config.js
//
// That was not a bad Vite config and not an auth/permission problem. With no
// wrangler configuration in the repository, Wrangler could not tell what to
// deploy, so it fell back to its **autoconfig** path and tried to detect a
// framework. It identified this project as Vite (vite.config.js + the Vite
// dependency), and Vite's detector asks "does this Vite config use the
// Cloudflare plugin?" by running the file through Wrangler's own *JSONC*
// parser. `vite.config.js` is JavaScript, so the parse failed and Wrangler
// aborted before it ever looked at the repository contents.
//
// Declaring the deployment target here means autoconfig never runs: Wrangler
// reads this file, and nothing in it is guessed from vite.config.js.
//
// WHAT THIS DEPLOYS — AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
//
// This repository contains exactly ONE Cloudflare-compatible artifact: the
// built static frontend (`npm run build` → ./dist). This file deploys that, as
// Workers Static Assets.
//
// It does NOT deploy the campaign send worker in ./worker. That worker is
// FastAPI + uvicorn on top of `smtplib.SMTP_SSL`, a background consumer thread
// and a file-backed settings store. Cloudflare Workers cannot run it:
//   * no raw TCP sockets  → smtplib / ssl cannot open an SMTP connection at all;
//   * no long-lived process or threads → no queue consumer loop, no heartbeat;
//   * no writable filesystem → services/storage.py and the .env reader fail;
//   * fastapi / uvicorn / pydantic / httpx / python-dotenv are not part of the
//     Pyodide-based Python Workers runtime.
// SMTP delivery is the worker's entire purpose, so this is a hard blocker, not
// a configuration detail. See the README section "Campaign execution and the
// send worker" for the host that is meant to run it.
//
// CONSEQUENCE OF DEPLOYING THE FRONTEND HERE
//
// A Cloudflare copy of the site is a static mirror only. It has no Gmail API
// (`/api/gmail/*` is a Vercel function) and no send worker, so Inbox, Compose,
// Sent and campaign delivery cannot work there. It is viable for previewing the
// UI; Vercel remains the production frontend. Do not point a user-facing domain
// at it.
//
// If you do not want a Cloudflare frontend deployment at all, deleting this
// file and removing the deploy command from the Cloudflare project returns the
// repository to having no Cloudflare configuration — which is also a valid
// state, since nothing here must run on Cloudflare.
//
// If you DO use it, set the build-time variables below in the Cloudflare
// project's build environment (names only; the values are the same public
// Vite values already set on Vercel):
//   VITE_SUPABASE_URL, VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, VITE_SITE_URL,
//   VITE_API_BASE_URL (optional), VITE_MAIL_WORKER_URL
// ============================================================================
{
  // Must match the Worker name in the Cloudflare project if you intend to
  // update that existing project rather than create a new Worker.
  "name": "seed-mail-frontend",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-10",

  // Static assets only: there is deliberately no "main" entry point, because
  // there is no Worker script in this repository to deploy.
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    // The SPA is hash-routed, so "/" and "/assets/*" are sufficient. This
    // matches the rewrite in vercel.json that keeps real deep links such as
    // /privacy working on refresh. A consequence worth knowing: an unknown
    // path (including /api/gmail/*) returns index.html, and the app already
    // reports that condition precisely rather than pretending the API answered.
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application"
  }
}
